        "startMs": 0,
        "text": "P = (3, 2). Sites: A (1, 1), B (7, 1), C (5, 6). Their readings are 15, 32 and 48. Which site's reading estimates P?",
        "endMs": 7000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-02",
        "startMs": 7000,
        "text": "On the Calculator page, enter (3 − 1)² + (2 − 1)². Close each bracket, tap x², then Enter. No square root is needed.",
        "endMs": 22000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-03",
        "startMs": 22000,
        "text": "Use the same P, but subtract B’s coordinates: (3 − 7)² + (2 − 1)². A negative difference becomes positive when squared.",
        "endMs": 36000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-04",
        "startMs": 36000,
        "text": "Now use C: (3 − 5)² + (2 − 6)². Compare all the results, not just A and B.",
        "endMs": 50000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-05",
        "startMs": 50000,
        "text": "The squared distances are A: 5, B: 17, C: 20. Site A is nearest. The estimate at P is A’s reading, 15, not an average.",
        "endMs": 57000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-06",
        "startMs": 57000,
        "text": "Now move P to (4, 2). Its offsets from A are 3 and 1; from B they are −3 and 1. Enter 3² + 1² to check both.",
        "endMs": 67000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-07",
        "startMs": 67000,
        "text": "For C the offsets are −1 and −4. Enter (−1)² + (−4)², using the negative key inside each bracket.",
        "endMs": 79000
      },
      {
        "id": "watch-08",
        "startMs": 79000,
        "text": "A and B tie at 10; C is farther at 17. This point lies on their cell boundary. With readings 15 and 32, no unique estimate exists unless a tie-break rule is given.",
        "endMs": 87000
      }
